ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2];OUT=ROOT/'outputs/pitch-benchmark';load=lambda p:json.loads((OUT/p).read_text())
ptdb=load('summary.json');avid=load('avid-padded-summary.json');gate=load('noise-common-gate.json');ag=load('avid-common-gate.json');manifest=load('avid/scoring-manifest.json');figures=[]
for ident in ['sp4_s1_sen1_soft','sp11_s1_sen1_soft','sp12_s1_sen1_normal','sp14_s1_sen2_normal']:
 c=next(c for c in manifest['clips'] if c['id']==ident);ref=json.loads((ROOT/c['reference']).read_text());fig,ax=plt.subplots(figsize=(11,3.5),layout='constrained')
 for suffix,color,label in [('app-stream','#c65a15','Current Soundglow detector'),('stock-filtered-stream','#217a4c','Standard filtered AC, streamed'),('swift-stream','#6656b8','SwiftF0, streamed')]:
  d=load('avid-padded-streams/'+ident+'-'+suffix+'.json');ax.plot([r['time'] for r in d['rows']],[r['hz'] if r['hz'] else np.nan for r in d['rows']],color=color,lw=1.2,alpha=.8,label=label)
 anchors=[r for r in ref if not r.get('exclude')];ax.scatter([r['time'] for r in anchors],[r['hz'] for r in anchors],s=8,c='black',label='Independent EGG-derived anchors',zorder=8);ax.set(title=ident,xlabel='Seconds in original excerpt',ylabel='Hz',ylim=(50,None));ax.grid(alpha=.2);ax.legend(fontsize=8,loc='upper right');name=ident+'.png';fig.savefig(OUT/name,dpi=150);plt.close(fig);figures.append((ident,name))
def table(headers,rows):return '<table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+html.escape(str(h))+'</th>' for h in headers)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+html.escape(str(v))+'</td>' for v in r)+'</tr>' for r in rows)+'</tbody></table>'
names={'app-corroborated':'Current Soundglow detector','app-stream':'Current Soundglow detector','app-raw':'App raw AC','app-filtered':'App filtered AC','praat-stock-raw':'Stock Praat raw (offline)','praat-stock-filtered':'Stock Praat filtered (offline)','swift-f0':'SwiftF0 (offline)','reaper':'REAPER (offline)','stock-filtered-stream':'Standard filtered AC, streamed','swift-stream':'SwiftF0, streamed'}
pct=lambda x:'—' if x is None else f'{100*x:.1f}%'
pt=table(['Detector','Pitch F1@50c','Missed voiced seconds','Pitch in reference-unvoiced seconds'],[[names[g['method']],pct(g['f1_50']),f"{g['missed']*.01:.2f}",f"{g['falseVoiced']*.01:.2f}"] for g in ptdb['groups'] if g['origin']==.016 and g['split']=='test' and g['condition']=='all'])
av=table(['Streamed detector','Pitch F1@50c on EGG anchors','Gross-error frames (>20%)','Missing anchor frames','Max clip p95 audio delay'],[[names[g['method']],pct(g['f1_50']),g['grossFrames'],g['missed'],f"{g['maxClipP95AvailabilityMs']:.0f}ms"] for g in avid['groups'] if g['condition']=='all'])
noise=table(['Condition','Detector (same VAD)','Correct voiced frames within50c','Gross-error frames','Pitch in reference-unvoiced seconds'],[[g['condition'],names[g['method']],pct(g['correct50']/g['voiced'] if g['voiced'] else None),g['grossFrames'],f"{g['falseVoiced']*.01:.2f}"] for g in gate['groups'] if g['gate']])
soft=table(['Condition','Detector (same VAD)','Correct EGG voiced anchors within50c','Missing anchors'],[[g['condition'],names[g['method']],pct(g['correct50']/g['voiced']),g['missed']] for g in ag['groups'] if g['gate'] and g['condition'] in ['soft','normal']])
sensitivity=table(['Reference first centre','Current detector F1','Stock filtered offline F1','SwiftF0 offline F1'],[[str(round(origin*1000))+'ms',*[pct(next(g['f1_50'] for g in ptdb['groups'] if g['origin']==origin and g['split']=='test' and g['condition']=='all' and g['method']==method)) for method in ['app-corroborated','praat-stock-filtered','swift-f0']]] for origin in [0,.016,.032]])
page='''<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"><title>Soundglow: broader pitch benchmark</title><style>body{font:17px/1.55 system-ui;max-width:1100px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 20px;color:#17212b;background:#fafbfd}h1,h2{line-height:1.2}h2{margin-top:2em}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px;margin:18px 0}td,th{padding:9px;border-bottom:1px solid #ccd3dd;text-align:left}th{background:#e7edf4}img{max-width:100%}a{color:#145ab5}.note{padding:18px;background:#edf1f5;border-left:4px solid #51759b}code{font-size:.9em}section{overflow:auto}</style>
<h1>Soundglow: broader pitch benchmark</h1><p>Local research run,20October2026. Production detector frozen atcdf3adb. No app changes, commits or deployment.</p>
<p class="note"><b>Decision: retain the current detector for now.</b> Neither candidate dominates. Standard filtered autocorrelation reduces gross pitch errors at the same observed delay, but increases false pitched output under noise. SwiftF0 brings no decisive independent advantage and roughly doubles audio-availability delay. This supports a separate, bounded speech/voicing-gate experiment rather than another private-recording threshold tweak.</p>
<h2>What was tested</h2><ul><li>400original PTDB utterances/20speakers:160development,80calibration,160evaluation. Only non-shared si prompts; old16pilot utterances excluded.</li><li>64new AVID excerpts/8new speakers,4male/4female, soft/normal/loud/veryloud. Raw microphone and EGG cropped synchronously; released snippets locate the excerpts. EGG anchor reference covers2,840of7,269frames (39.1%). All other frames are unknown, not silence.</li><li>20PTDB originals across20speakers with20/10dB changing household noise, plus3noise-only controls. These are derived stress cases, not40additional independent recordings. Noise SNR is relative to reference-voiced speech RMS. Only3distinct5second noise sources; not a general real-world-noise benchmark.</li><li>Current app raw/filtered/corroborated modes; stock Praat raw/filtered; SwiftF0v0.3.0; REAPER. Additional research-only stock-filtered bridge uses documented scoring settings with10ms hop and50–800Hz range in the same bounded stream context.</li></ul>
<h2>Broad corpus screen</h2><p>PTDB evaluation split only, nominal16ms reference origin. Confidence thresholds are fixed, not optimized on evaluation. This table mixes whole-file and bounded-stream context, so it is a screen rather than a deployment ranking. PTDB is known SwiftF0 training overlap: its evaluation split is not a neural held-out claim.</p>'''+pt+'''
<h2>Independent streamed comparison</h2><p>All candidates receive identical100ms packets,0.5s of silence before/after each excerpt, and the complete original excerpt is scored. That represents an already-running microphone stream without letting end-of-file flush improve only one algorithm. The original short-snippet test exaggerated quiet-speech losses through stream startup/tail effects; the corrected result below supersedes it. F1 uses50cent tolerance; gross errors use>20%relative pitch error.</p>'''+av+soft+'''
<p>Paired speaker-bootstrap95%intervals for F1 change versus current: standard filtered +0.44percentage points, interval[-0.54,+1.62]; SwiftF0−0.36points, interval[-2.47,+1.47]. Neither establishes an overall independent improvement. Standard filtered does roughly halve gross-error frames72→34, but those errors and false-voicing costs must be considered separately.</p>
<h2>Noise and speech gating</h2><p>Same shipped WebRTC/libfvad gate for all candidates, with the same100ms trailing/30ms future evidence policy; only decisions already available when a pitch frame is emitted can count. No renderer smoothing or line confirmation is scored. AVID lacks complete unvoiced labels, so false-voicing claims come from PTDB and known non-speech controls, not from missing AVID anchors.</p>'''+noise+'''
<h2>Timing evidence and uncertainty</h2><p>The official PTDB extraction script specifies32ms windows/10ms hops; Snack documents the ESPS first row at half the window, giving16ms. An independent laryngograph NCC diagnostic used development speakers only and was broadly consistent with that support. It is not a per-detector offset fit, and the32ms analysis window cannot establish instantaneous pitch at exact transition boundaries. Reference transition bands±30ms are excluded and counted.</p>'''+sensitivity+'''
<p>The table is sensitive to clock choice; this is a material evidence limitation, not a reason to choose whichever offset helps a candidate. EGG-derived AVID anchors have their own explicit raw-sample clock and do not inherit the PTDB convention.</p>
<h2>Example curves</h2><p>These fixed examples were selected by speaker/task, not by which model wins. Black points are high-confidence EGG-derived anchors, not complete manually corrected truth. Gaps in black points mean unknown.</p>'''+''.join('<figure><img src="'+name+'" alt="'+ident+' pitch comparison"><figcaption>'+ident+'</figcaption></figure>' for ident,name in figures)+'''
<h2>What this does not establish</h2><ul><li>No high-confidence reference frames above400Hz occur in either selected set. Genuine high-register speech preservation remains untested, even with louder AVID controls. Synthetic high-tone tests validate plumbing, not that product claim.</li><li>EGG anchors require NCC>.9 plus derivative-pulse agreement≤50c and interval variation≤10%; ambiguous, irregular or weak EGG frames are excluded. This can favor easier voicing. Synthetic-period/silence/noise tests pass, but the reference is not a fully manually corrected corpus.</li><li>These are detector outputs. The complete current product also applies speech detection, temporal confirmation/grouping and drawing. Smooth lines are not accuracy evidence.</li><li>Latency is audio availability with100ms packets on an AppleM2Ultra. Inference, UI/audio capture, rendering, loading, battery and thermal behavior on phones are not established. No physical iPhone/Android tests were performed; no mobile-device connection was available through the checked developer tools.</li><li>SwiftF0's public training configuration lists PTDB/MOCHA/CMUArctic, not AVID. AVID is an external check relative to that disclosed list, not proof of undisclosed training provenance.</li></ul>
<h2>Next decision</h2><p>Keep production fixed. Evaluate one stronger speech/voicing gate against the current gate using the frozen detector and this benchmark, adding continuous real-device speech and genuine high speech before a release decision. Standard filtered AC remains a useful low-latency comparison, not an automatic replacement. Physical phone validation remains required before shipping a new model.</p>
<h2>Sources and artifacts</h2><p><a href="https://www2.spsc.tugraz.at/databases/PTDB-TUG/DOCUMENTATION/PTDB-TUG_REPORT.pdf">PTDB original report/extraction script</a> · <a href="https://npg.dl.ac.uk/MIDAS/manual/ActiveTcl8.4.4.0-html/snack/tcl-man.html">Snack manual</a> · <a href="https://zenodo.org/records/10524873">AVID official data</a> · <a href="https://github.com/lars76/swift-f0">SwiftF0</a> · <a href="https://github.com/lars76/swift-f0-training/blob/main/config.py">Training configuration</a> · <a href="https://github.com/google/REAPER">REAPER</a></p><p><a href="summary.json">Full corpus scores</a> · <a href="avid-padded-summary.json">Corrected independent streaming scores</a> · <a href="noise-common-gate.json">Noise/gating scores</a> · <a href="ptdb/timing-audit.json">EGG timing diagnostic</a></p>'''
